 "schema": "explicit_statistics_cohorts_v1",
 "purpose": "Wild-type cohorts for which the explicit evolutionary statistics (plmc Potts, official GEMME) are produced. One descriptor per cohort; the R1 mutation-effect ladder is one instance of the same descriptor rather than a hard-wired default.",
 "protocol": {
  "max_sequences": 5000,
  "max_sequences_rule": "R1's own depth cap, applied by R1's own rule: best HSP per subject, at least 80% query coverage, ordered by descending bit score, cut at the cap. The cap is a descriptor field so that every cohort states the depth it was built at; it is never read from a retained profile store.",
  "profile_store_role": "cross-check only. The alignment is rebuilt from the raw hit table, so a store built at a different cap changes nothing in the produced features; it is compared against the rebuild only where neither cap binds.",
  "search_depth_limitation": "A cohort inherits the retrieval depth of the DIAMOND search that produced its hit table. R1 searched at --max-target-seqs 5000, the later cohorts at 10000. For a wild type whose coverage-passing subject count exceeds 5000 the two are not the same candidate pool, and that difference cannot be removed without re-running the search. It is declared per cohort and counted per wild type.",
  "refusal_rule": "A wild type with fewer than two retained homolog rows carries no Potts model and no GEMME run. It is enumerated as a refusal with its reason in the export and in the contract, never imputed and never silently dropped."
 },
